  "notes": [
    "Thirteenth single-TU promotion on this line, and the same shape as ov045/daObjKm2_Ami_Bou_c next door: a dBgActor_c subclass whose TU owns its own key function and therefore emits its vtable and RTTI.",
    "The class was coined FireSeaElevator until the rename immediately before this promotion. The cartridge spells it at ov045:0x02112cb0/0x02112cbc, and promotion needs that name: the compiler's _ZTS bytes have to equal the cartridge's, which no coined spelling can achieve.",
    "daObjKm2_Agaru_c_classInit's vptr store is (int)&_ZTV16daObjKm2_Agaru_c[2], not the bare symbol. Once the TU emits the vtable, mwcc's symbol is the storage start at 0x02112cec and the ROM stores the address point eight bytes later. Every byte gate is blind to this -- a relocated word is a wildcard -- and objisolate's addend check is what catches it.",
    "The destructor is defined inline in include/daObjKm2_Agaru_c.h and declared first in the class body. Out of line, mwccarm emits D2/D0/D1 while the cartridge holds D1 (0x021111a0) then D0 (0x021111e4) and no D2 at all, and objisolate refuses the object for emitting out of ROM address order.",
    "func_ov045_021114a8 and func_ov045_021114c8 are this TU's file-local dBgW callbacks. The legacy pair disagreed about func_ov045_021114c8's arity -- the definition took three parameters, InitResources declared it as two -- which no single TU can hold; the three-parameter definition is kept and InitResources takes its address through an int cast, exactly as the ROM does.",
    "The four fields above dBgActor_c's 0x320 end are named from behaviour rather than padded over: mRestY latches the spawn height, mDelayTimer counts the 0x14-frame hold at each end, mRidden is set by func_ov045_021114a8 and cleared every frame, mState drives Behavior's switch. Offsets, types and the 0x328 span are unchanged from the padded declaration.",
    "daObjKm2_Agaru_c_classInit and g_profile_KM2_AGARU are reconstructed source-style names: SM64DS proves the RTTI class, KM2_AGARU registry ID, descriptor/factory relationship, allocation size, and vtable identity; later EAD lineage supplies the spelling prior. Historical aliases were daObjKm2_Agaru_c_Spawn and daObjKm2_Agaru_c_SpawnInfo."
  ],
